# Two-point calibration of the gripper's mm reading: raw motor reading -> jaw gap
# (PROJECT_SPEC.md "2026-10-24 — Gripper release, hold and calibration").
# The gripper motor must be released (/arm/gripper_release) so the jaws can be set by hand.
#   step "closed": the jaws pushed fully shut by hand -> the raw reading now is gap 0
#   step "open":   the jaws held open at a caliper-measured gap_m -> the raw reading now is gap_m; with the
#                  closed point recorded, the new mapping is applied at once and saved to the calibration
#                  file (gripper_calib_file; the previous one backed up)
#   step "cancel": forget a recorded closed point
string step
float64 gap_m
---
bool success
string message
float64 raw_m             # the raw reading recorded (closed / open)
float64 travel_m          # the new mapping (step "open", success): raw reading at gap 0
float64 scale             # jaw gap per raw metre
float64 max_gap_m         # the widest gap the motor's stroke gives
